melband-roformer (0.1.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * app/requirements.txt, app/pyproject.toml, debian/rules,
    scripts/build-appimage.sh: bump the pinned CUDA wheel channel from
    cu126 to cu130 and torch from 2.11.0 to 2.13.0 (current PyTorch
    stable as of this release). cu130 is the channel PyTorch itself now
    treats as the stable default (the unsuffixed build published to
    PyPI since the 2.11 release series); cu126 remains available
    upstream only as a fallback for older drivers and is slated for
    removal entirely from PyTorch 2.15.
  * torchaudio deliberately left at ==2.11.0, not bumped alongside
    torch: upstream put torchaudio into maintenance mode at that
    release (its final release to date) and documents it as compatible
    with later torch minors without itself needing a rebuild -- there
    is no 2.12.x/2.13.x torchaudio to pin to.
  * app/melband_roformer_wrapper/gpuinfo.py: raise MIN_DRIVER_VERSION /
    MIN_DRIVER_VERSION_STR from 560.28.03 to 580.65.06 (CUDA 13.0 GA
    linux driver floor) to match the cu130 bump above. Note this is a
    new major-branch floor, not a point bump: CUDA 13.x raised the
    minimum required driver from the 12.x family's >=525 up to >=580.
    Also genericized _min_driver_ok()'s docstring (previously
    hardcoded "cu126 wheels") so it no longer needs editing on future
    channel bumps.
  * README.md, README.debian.md: updated all pinned-version references
    (dependency list, --info sample output, CUDA-compatibility section)
    to match, and documented the torchaudio maintenance-mode reasoning
    inline for future bumps.
  * No source/CLI code changes needed beyond the above:
    melband-roformer-infer==0.1.5 only requires torch>=2.0, so it is
    unaffected by the torch 2.11.0 -> 2.13.0 bump.

